#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114948 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeafe81f-2d40-5413-8d19-881972161400" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Output of an Exponential Decay Function"}] :question/id #uuid "df739a77-559a-53ed-ad04-be16403b9f46" :question/math-academy-id "e-2076" :question/problem "The value of a certain stock, in dollars, decays according to the formula\n\n$$\nV(t)= 4\\, 500\\cdot (0.85)^t,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the stock was bought. \n\nI. What does $V(3)$ mean in this context?\n\nII. Calculate $V(2) - V(3),$ and determine its meaning in this context." :question/worked-solution "- The value $V(3)$ represents the value of the function $V(t)$ at $t=3.$ In this context, it represents the value of the stock $3$ years after the initial investment.\n\n- By similar reasoning to the above, $V(2)$ represents the stock's value $2$ years after the initial investment. Therefore, the expression\n\n$$\nV(2) - V(3)\n$$\n\nrepresents the total reduction in the value of the stock between $t=2$ and $t=3$ years since the initial investment.\n\nNow, let's compute its value. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(2)-V(3) & =4\\,500\\cdot (0.85)^{2}-4\\,500\\cdot (0.85)^{3} \\\\  & =487.6874 \\\\  & ≈488,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer. Therefore, the value of the stock dropped by $\\[math]488$ between years $2$ and $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114949 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0f5949-6a1a-5187-a246-8f9bac2e8d58" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting a Decay Rate"}] :question/id #uuid "d550f36c-a6f0-5b37-a998-4d44fa5f1d3d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2078" :question/problem "The market value ![](images/93/93636eb5ea1d6d8df4d0390651023dd9a4aa32ff9077d3edca03c6a4d2593c9f.svg) of a car, in dollars, ![](images/70/707bb132def3690d81bf1f0c8cf416c1382322ab19d66264cdab1decc4669307.svg) years since it was first purchased depreciates according to the following rule: \n![](images/9e/9eab3a81e5055a62b6e3dbba458b267fadf4ebdfe44786f23259fabc3d1cd409.svg)\n\nWhat does the base of the exponential expression ![](images/d6/d660f48227bd14736021adeb26de738a61fe583d94bc205ead8a5bab1c1acb61.svg) mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form ![](images/52/527f98e7ede20d48ea37c58afcb0d4489fa5ad6651f21e3a7d1c08f5e3bb76ac.svg) where\n\n- ![](images/b6/b6cceb36174e4439694c8b988c00019d9707a7b6377e0c806c51c8d330e0ab4b.svg) represents the initial value of the car (in dollars).\n\n- ![](images/ef/ef47ff747a4899500bf1cdaa584e477954cd417238e8b7e695862da9b0022c6a.svg) where ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) is the decay rate.\n\n- ![](images/70/707bb132def3690d81bf1f0c8cf416c1382322ab19d66264cdab1decc4669307.svg) is the time since the car was first purchased, in years.\n\nSolving for the decay rate ![](images/22/22d9393dcae7cd46f7da8986fc4764e2f14e127fb9dcdf114770ad2de2f6b098.svg) we get\n\n![](images/64/64161e1a2f19b6bdb3f7651e8a553179126ccf33901d20311347dbd9ff98aaab.svg)\n\nNow, ![](images/85/85eb3227c042f8ec4de535b2fb7fc37c5cd34735961e5ba26e6a511eff5707b5.svg) (expressed as a percent) is equal to ![](images/92/92e44f079247c93011878456e1294adc24fe51c089fd07e12107f1ad75e2d91d.svg) \n\nSo, the base of the exponential expression ![](images/55/551172a22e640525b7b69ef43cab353b50dd3ca6123574a3dd5df79475ea5496.svg) means that the value of the car depreciates by ![](images/41/414c7a992cb07b0cf60bef2446dc3eb4072aeb99acedf6d77c02b5c183cdfc63.svg) each year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114950 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115385 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab694f0f-947f-5bba-ad7a-988ea28a97fd" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Exponential Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "795b2573-6738-5fbd-a0f4-9d94eff7aee7" :question/math-academy-id "e-2079" :question/problem "A house was purchased for $\\[math]90\\,000.$ Shortly after purchasing the property, the owners discovered widening cracks in the foundation. As a result, the value of the property is reduced by one-half every year. What does the expression $\\[/math]\\,90\\,000\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^6$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t) = a \\cdot b^t,$ where we have the following:\n\n- $a=90\\,000$ represents the purchase price of the property.\n\n- $b = \\dfrac 1 2$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t = 6$ the time, in years, since the property was bought.\n\nSince $t=6,$ the expression $\\[math]\\,90\\,000\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^6$ gives the value of the property after $6$ years."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115385 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab694f0f-947f-5bba-ad7a-988ea28a97fd" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Exponential Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bedd74b-c037-5d37-8e5f-1cba0a6bb7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There were $75$ reservations per night initially" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508405} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bd5f77-7ec1-5bab-b04b-3f9ff06d4e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There were $75$ reservations per night each month in $2020$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508685} {:answer/id #uuid "e8038edb-8fa3-5906-a2f7-a4795323716f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of reservations per night increased by $75$ each year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508758} {:answer/id #uuid "f23ec721-40a9-5e3e-97ba-f085f6149342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of reservations per night decreased by $75$ each year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508782} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e554fa-e8b6-5704-866b-b331bc16cd1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There were $75$ reservations per night $9$ months after March $2020$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bedd74b-c037-5d37-8e5f-1cba0a6bb7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There were $75$ reservations per night initially" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508405} :answer-field/id #uuid "ade6f4de-4aa6-5980-a9cd-b629e28dce38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a99e73a5-2dae-5b2f-a4fd-53ba3d7abecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-112449" :question/problem "Due to a quarantine initiated in March $2020$, the number of reservations per night in a hotel decreased by one-quarter each month. By the end of $2020,$ the number of reservations per night decreased to $75\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{9}.$ What does the factor $75$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot {b}^{t}$, where we have the following:\n\n- $a=75$ represents the initial number of reservations per night.\n\n- $b=\\frac{3}{4}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=9$ is the time, in months, since March $2020.$\n\nSince $a=75,$ this indicates that there were $75$ reservations initially."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeafe81f-2d40-5413-8d19-881972161400" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Output of an Exponential Decay Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c797564-dac6-5eb1-9127-ab310ef8c78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$113.4$ milligrams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508624} {:answer/id #uuid "d24c93c8-1dc6-5d91-94ea-78f93185c722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$126$ milligrams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508729} {:answer/id #uuid "db2ae0a7-f5fd-53f5-a329-0691e24fa0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$102.06$ milligrams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508740} {:answer/id #uuid "eff17da3-f67e-5378-acc1-934fd0f5f227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11.34$ milligrams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508776} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b02a77-2883-57bb-aa83-9fb226ae367c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ milligrams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eff17da3-f67e-5378-acc1-934fd0f5f227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11.34$ milligrams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508776} :answer-field/id #uuid "73fafd4e-edd5-5743-8519-b748f97293c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bce8526b-2382-5fd4-882b-274b4364bd61" :question/math-academy-id "q-112525" :question/problem "The caffeine level, in milligrams, in a patient's bloodstream $t$ hours after drinking a cup of coffee is given by the function $C(t)=140\\cdot {(0.9)}^{t}.$ How much caffeine is metabolized between the second and third hour after drinking the coffee?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the level of caffeine in the blood between $t=2$ and $t=3$ hours after drinking a cup of coffee. To calculate this, we find the level of caffeine in the blood after $2$ hours, and we subtract from it the level of caffeine in the blood after $3$ hours. So we need to evaluate\n\n$$\nC(2)-C(3).\n$$\n\nThe level of caffeine in the blood after $2$ hours is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(2) & =140\\cdot {(0.9)}^{2} \\\\  & =140\\cdot 0.81 \\\\  & =113.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe level of caffeine in the blood after $3$ hours is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(3) & =140\\cdot {(0.9)}^{3} \\\\  & =140\\cdot 0.729 \\\\  & =102.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the level of caffeine metabolized between $t=2$ and $t=3$ hours after drinking a cup of coffee is\n\n$$\n113.4-102.06=11.34.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115385 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab694f0f-947f-5bba-ad7a-988ea28a97fd" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Exponential Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de488ef-505a-500b-ad78-f583f6144c09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The mass of the sample decreases by $12$ grams every hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508504} {:answer/id #uuid "ab312762-790a-5e64-a63c-e1d4cb623633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sample's mass at the beginning of the observations was $12$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508650} {:answer/id #uuid "af234de8-eaa1-5aa9-92f0-3abd4d8f2279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The mass of the sample will always be at least $12$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508655} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b43987-37f7-5364-b35f-58555cc0100d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The mass of the sample increases by  $12$ grams every hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508701} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f1b31a-5249-57a7-91f8-34f57014c41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The mass of the sample decreases by $12$ grams every $5$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab312762-790a-5e64-a63c-e1d4cb623633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The sample's mass at the beginning of the observations was $12$ grams" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508650} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e6cc398-d3e6-51a5-bca6-28d64f2320a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a686be2-6ff3-542b-aec0-e3ca1a18babf" :question/math-academy-id "q-64117" :question/problem "A scientist observes that the mass, in grams, of a particular substance decays exponentially according to the rule  $12\\cdot (0.5)^{t},$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the beginning of observations.  What does the factor $12$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot {b}^{t},$ where we have the following:\n\n- $a=12$ represents the initial mass of the sample.\n\n- $b=0.5$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t$ is the time since the beginning of the observations, in hours.\n\nSince $a=12,$ this indicates that the sample's mass at the beginning of the observations was  $12$ grams."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeafe81f-2d40-5413-8d19-881972161400" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Output of an Exponential Decay Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6168c3-ec73-5842-ac0b-41e0e64d2017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of the boat after $4$ years is $$7\\,290.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508479} {:answer/id #uuid "571af005-5fac-5ee1-92d0-b458708d0ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of the boat depreciates by $$\\,10\\,000$ every four years" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508517} {:answer/id #uuid "682f9c50-f1ca-51af-837c-a05b5dbf2539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of the boat after $4$ years is $$10\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508544} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bdc9c1-3109-5c94-87c8-c835fb3e0d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of the boat after $4$ years is $$5\\,901.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508666} {:answer/id #uuid "bac5181e-4303-5faa-80ee-d64ecc1d0d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of the boat after $4$ years is $$6\\,561.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac5181e-4303-5faa-80ee-d64ecc1d0d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The value of the boat after $4$ years is $$6\\,561.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508671} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94aa7fe-c122-5d2e-afea-03c77be24593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d33dc350-97af-5862-9547-76e026eaf801" :question/math-academy-id "q-64120" :question/problem "The value of a boat, in dollars, depreciates according to the function $p(t)=10\\,000\\cdot {(0.9)}^{t},$ where $t$ is the number of years since the boat was purchased. Calculate $p(4),$ and determine its meaning in this context." :question/worked-solution "The value $p(4)$ represents the value of $p(t)$ at $t=4.$ In this context, it represents the value of the boat $4$ years after it was purchased.\n\nSubstituting $t=4$ into the expression for $p(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(4) & =10\\,000\\cdot {(0.9)}^{4} \\\\  & =10\\,000\\cdot (0.656\\,1) \\\\  & =6\\,561.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of the boat after four years is $$6,561.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0f5949-6a1a-5187-a246-8f9bac2e8d58" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting a Decay Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19383a11-e51a-5394-8c61-b649e6bdd6a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The population of ticks decreases by $30%$ every week" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508429} {:answer/id #uuid "556e5656-5915-5883-a0df-bf099080f624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The population of ticks decreases by $70%$ every week" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508515} {:answer/id #uuid "97a9c6fb-5cd4-57fa-9e3d-7809fba02632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The population of ticks increases by $70%$ every week" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508617} {:answer/id #uuid "beffae14-374a-5cc1-afc4-57fb68a71704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The population of ticks increases by $30%$ every week" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508679} {:answer/id #uuid "c5cace87-2dbe-5012-8bc0-2f5187cf6ad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There were $70$ ticks initially" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19383a11-e51a-5394-8c61-b649e6bdd6a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The population of ticks decreases by $30%$ every week" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508429} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c41047d-dc64-5d42-b2e6-178103fc1b49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "836a9482-113e-597c-80f8-a8ed0a6b01c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-85526" :question/problem "Due to acaricides, the population of ticks in a certain park decreases according to the expression $20\\,000\\cdot (0.7)^{t},$ where $t$ is the time, in weeks, since acaricides were first applied. What does the base of the exponential expression $(0.7)$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot (1-r)^{t},$ where:\n\n- $a=20\\,000$ represents the initial number of ticks.\n\n- $1-r=0.7,$ where $r$ is the decay rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time, in weeks, since the acaricides were first applied.\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n1-r=0.7\\,⟹\\,r=0.3.\n$$\n\nNow, $0.3$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $30%.$ \n\nSo, the base of the exponential expression $0.7$ means that the population of ticks decreases by $30%$ every week."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0f5949-6a1a-5187-a246-8f9bac2e8d58" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting a Decay Rate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f2fd4bc-8ad8-5931-940b-12d788278a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of customers decreases by $83%$ every day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508442} {:answer/id #uuid "5b462848-a0e5-5c5d-9e8b-6adbac840b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of customers increases by $17%$ every day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508525} {:answer/id #uuid "62598ce9-1c57-55c6-9267-929be01338ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of customers increases by $83%$ every day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508538} {:answer/id #uuid "842fdb7d-aaed-5236-a16e-8730aca130cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of customers decreases by $17%$ every day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508585} {:answer/id #uuid "bf65f838-2329-5424-bfb0-efc4aa5e22da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There were $83$ customers initially." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "842fdb7d-aaed-5236-a16e-8730aca130cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of customers decreases by $17%$ every day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508585} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aec91ab-d82d-5f67-b158-63b64417a2fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a688991-2eb3-5f8d-836d-4a680ceee3ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-85527" :question/problem "The daily number of customers to a particular cafe declines according to the expression $500\\cdot (0.83)^{t}$, where $t$ is the number of days since the local news reported that the cafe did not pass a health inspection. \nWhat does the base of the exponential expression $(0.83)$ mean in this context?" :question/worked-solution "The given expression is an exponential decay expression of the form $y(t)=a\\cdot (1-r)^{t},$ where:\n\n- $a=500$ represents the initial number of customers.\n\n- $1-r=0.83,$ where $r$ is the decay rate.\n\n- $t$ is the time in days since the local news reported that the cafe did not pass a health inspection.\n\nSolving for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n1-r=0.83\\,⟹\\,r=0.17.\n$$\n\nNow, $0.17$ (expressed as a percent) is equal to $17%.$ \n\nSo, the base of the exponential expression $0.83$ means that the number of customers decreases by $17%$ every day."}]}
